Source tree layout
------------------

This package is maintained using "git-buildpackage". The git
repository includes upstream sources as well as the debian/ directory,
with patches unapplied.

There exists a delta between the upstream git repository and their
official tarballs. This package builds against the upstream tarballs
and not against their git tree. The upstream tree in the packaging git
repository is only there for documentation purposes and the package
will not build against it.

Building from source
--------------------

The recommended way to build this package is the following, from an
empty directory:

  git clone git@salsa.debian.org:debian/opendnssec.git
  cd opendnssec
  uscan -dd
  gbp buildpackage --git-export-dir=.. --git-overlay

It is advised to build in a clean environment, using pbuilder, docker,
or something similar.

Building a source package
-------------------------

The recommended way to build a source package from the repository is
the following, assuming a build from the master branch of a clean
repository:

  uscan -dd
  gbp buildpackage --git-export-dir=.. --git-overlay \
                   --git-builder="dpkg-source -b ."

